# CITATION.cff - how to cite this repository (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# GitHub reads this file and shows "Cite this repository" in the sidebar:
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-citation-files
# Format: https://citation-file-format.github.io/
# No "license" key: CFF reads a list of licenses as a choice (OR), but here
# code is MIT and prose is CC BY 4.0 (AND, by part). README.md explains it.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, please cite it as below. Code is under the
  MIT License (LICENSE) and prose under CC BY 4.0 (LICENSE-docs).
title: Hello World in many programming languages
type: software
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-22
authors:
  - family-names: Hamerski
    given-names: Eduardo
abstract: >-
  A teaching repository that writes the Hello World program in many
  programming languages, as a command-line program, a desktop window, a
  web app and, for a few languages, a mobile app, with the history, milestones, market usage and importance of
  each language. Every fact is cited and every program has install, build
  and run scripts that explain each step.
keywords:
  - hello world
  - programming languages
  - teaching
  - history of computing
  - programming paradigms
